@tradition cook-along
// Cook-along (0.60.7, the user's pick): Brennan's deputy, Lukas Dlamini, teaches one simple dish at the galley pass on
// Thursdays after dinner; you stir, taste, and get a portion.
k: 449
title: Cook-along
when: weekly thursday
at: 19:30-20:15
min: 25
where: 3 room Mess hall: mess-seat
hold: none
who: dlamini-lukas always, galley 25%, lingers-at-meals 35%, everyone 10%
anim: talk
host: dlamini-lukas
from: dlamini-lukas

== mail
- Cook-along tomorrow, {time}, at the galley pass. One simple dish, start to finish. You stir, you taste, you take a portion home.

== ask
- Cook-along tonight. Lukas says it's dumplings. I can't fold a dumpling.   #funny
- Learn a dish at the galley pass later? Lukas is a good teacher.   #warm
- Cook-along after dinner. Bring an apron, or borrow one.

== here
- Stir, don't splash. Stir.   #funny
- A pinch. No, a smaller pinch.
- Taste it now. Then taste it again in a minute. See?   #warm

== thanks
- Lukas shows you one simple dish at the galley pass. You stir, taste, and take away a warm portion of your own.   #warm

== chatter
- I made Lukas's soup in my cabin's kettle. Don't tell Brennan.   #funny
- Cook-along's dumplings were better than mine at home. Don't tell my mum.   #funny
